SUMMARY:Dormition panigiri of Panagia Episkopi\, Mesa Gonia
LOCATION:Mesa Gonia (Episkopi Gonias)\, Santorini\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The 11th-century Byzantine church of Panagia Episkopi at Mesa Gonia hosts the island's largest panigiri: on the evening of 14 August big cauldrons of fava and beans are cooked in the courtyard\, and after the liturgy on the 15th everyone eats free and dances to live island music with locals and summer visitors mixed together. Park along the Kamari road and walk up\; it gets very busy after 21:00.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/santorini/#mesa-gonia-episkopi-gonias-dormition-panigiri-of-panagia-epi
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/santorini/#mesa-gonia-episkopi-gonias-dormition-panigiri-of-panagia-epi
END:VEVENT
